fragments:
And broke on the mountain's brow;
It scattered the dusky fragments
All over the vale below.

fragile:
O haunting melody! thou art too slender,
Too fragile like a globe of crystal glass;
For all my stormy thoughts thou art too slender,

fray:
Chiding wailing voices that rang
Like a trumpet-call to the tug and fray;
And thus they sang:

frayed:
A half-length portrait, in a hanging cloak
Like one you wore once; ’tis a little frayed;
I pressed, too, for the nude harmonious arm—

frantically:
if I but pass they fall
back, frantically;
must always people mock?

frailest:
Into the weird depths of the hottest zone.
I will not quiver in the frailest bone,
You will not note a flicker of defeat;

fraught:
The first part was a tissue of hugged lies;
The second was its ruin fraught with pain:
Why raise the fair delusion to the skies

You say it is a fancied thing
Within my memory fraught;
To me it has a sacred place--
